@startuml sd_compensation_retry
title Scenario: a compensation that cannot be delivered (aircraft-maintenance down)

autonumber
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
actor "ATCC" as c
participant "flight-ops\nScheduleFlightUseCase" as uc
participant "SagaCompensation\nService" as comp
database "flights DB" as db
participant "airports-routes" as ar
participant "aircraft-maintenance" as am

c -> uc : POST /api/flights
note over uc : C2, C1, overlaps and C4 succeeded:\nthe aircraft is reserved
uc -> ar : C5 PUT /internal/flights/{id}
ar --> uc : 409 route not active
uc -> am : compensation: C4 PUT copy CANCELED
am --x uc : no answer (aircraft-maintenance down)
uc -> comp : recordFailedCompensation(copy CANCELED, AIRCRAFT)
comp -> db : store pending compensation
uc -> db : flight CANCELED
uc --> c : 409

loop every 5 s, while pending
  comp -> am : C4 PUT copy CANCELED
  alt delivered (200)
    comp -> db : remove pending compensation
  else still down
    comp -> db : keep it, try again later
  end
end

note over uc, am
  The copy CANCELED has a higher version than the copy SCHEDULED,
  and C4 is idempotent: delivering it late, or twice, is safe.
end note
@enduml
